# WorkPulse desktop agent — configuration.
#
#   cp .env.example .env    then fill in WP_COGNITO_CLIENT_ID
#
# The agent loads `.env` at startup (dotenvy). `.env` is gitignored; this example is committed.
# Real OS environment variables take precedence over `.env`.

# ── REQUIRED ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The Cognito App Client ID — the `UserPoolClientId` CDK stack output. Without it, login returns
# `auth:not_configured` and never reaches Cognito. (The app client must have USER_PASSWORD_AUTH
# enabled and the auth stack redeployed — see docs/RUNBOOK.md.)
WP_COGNITO_CLIENT_ID=

# ── Backend endpoint + region (defaults already target the live dev stack) ───
WP_INGEST_URL=https://oqlla6l5oc.execute-api.ap-south-1.amazonaws.com
WP_COGNITO_REGION=ap-south-1

# ── OPTIONAL ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Stable per-install agent id (dev override; otherwise a persisted UUID is minted).
# WP_AGENT_ID=

# Updater public key (minisign, from `cargo tauri signer generate`). Unset ⇒ updates disabled.
# WP_UPDATER_PUBKEY=

# Dev conveniences: skip autostart registration and/or the startup update check.
# WP_NO_AUTOSTART=1
# WP_NO_UPDATE=1

# Local agent-state dir (jsonl outbox, agent_id, screenshot temp files).
# WP_STATE_DIR=.agent-state
